SLOT: <%= @slot_key %> (<%= @day_label %>)

CANDIDATES (id | name | key ingredients | time | tags):
<%= for r <- @candidates do %>
<%= r.id %> | <%= r.title %> | <%= Enum.map_join(Enum.take(r.key_ingredients, 3), ", ", & &1) %> | <%= r.total_time_minutes %>m | <%= Enum.join(r.tags, " ") %><% end %>

WEEK CONTEXT (already assigned):
<%= if Enum.empty?(@assigned_context) do %>none<% else %><%= for c <- @assigned_context do %>
<%= c.slot_key %>: <%= c.title %><%= if c.leftover, do: " (leftover)", else: "" %><% end %><% end %>

PANTRY: <%= if Enum.empty?(@pantry), do: "none", else: Enum.join(@pantry, ", ") %>

DEALS THIS WEEK: <%= if Enum.empty?(@deals), do: "none", else: Enum.join(@deals, ", ") %>

RECENTLY COOKED (avoid these recipe_ids): <%= if Enum.empty?(@recent_recipe_ids), do: "none", else: Enum.join(@recent_recipe_ids, ", ") %>

EXCLUDED (already in the rule-based suggestions list — pick something different): <%= if Enum.empty?(@excluded_recipe_ids), do: "none", else: Enum.join(@excluded_recipe_ids, ", ") %>

Return JSON only — no prose, no markdown:
{"recipe_id": <int from CANDIDATES>, "reasoning": "<one short sentence explaining why>"}
